What you're welcome to do

You can download, install and play this mod, whether you got it from Steam Workshop or from its GitHub repository. You
can read the source to see how it works, change your own copy for your own games, and share screenshots, videos, links
and reviews. On GitHub you can view and fork the repository as GitHub's Terms of Service allow.

What needs my written permission first

Anything else you'd like to do with the code, art or text needs my written permission first. That includes uploading a
copy or a changed version anywhere (Steam Workshop, Nexus Mods, CivFanatics, another repository), copying parts of it
into another mod or project, and selling it or anything built from it.

Machine learning and AI

That permission also covers machine learning and AI uses. Using this work, in whole or in part, to train, fine-tune,
test or improve an AI or machine learning model, putting it in a dataset collected for that, or handing it to an AI
tool so the tool can reproduce or adapt it for another project all need my written permission, and I'm not giving it
at this time. Asking an AI tool to explain the mod, or to help with your own copy for your own games, is fine.

Text and data mining

I expressly reserve the rights to text and data mining of this work under Article 4(3) of Directive (EU) 2019/790 and
the national laws that put it into effect, including section 44b(3) of the German Copyright Act (UrhG). The
reservation applies to every copy of the work, wherever it's hosted or downloaded from.

Material under its own terms

base-standard/ui-next/screens/load-screen/load-screen-bootstrap.js is the game's own file with a few lines added at the
top so the loading screen shows the shuffle. The game's part of it belongs to Firaxis Games and 2K, and this license
covers only the added lines.

Rights that others already hold

This license covers what I hold rights in. Take-Two, Valve and GitHub each have rights under their own terms (the
Take-Two Terms of Service, the Steam Subscriber Agreement and the GitHub Terms of Service), and those stay as they
are.

Use at your own risk

The mod comes as it is, without any warranty. You use it at your own risk, and as far as the law allows, I'm not
liable for any harm that comes from using it, including lost or damaged saves.

Asking for permission

Open an issue on this mod's GitHub repository or message Tower on Steam. Permission counts when I've written back
saying yes to your specific use.
